<title>FRANCE: MOROCCO BUYS 90,000 TONNES SOFT WHEAT.</title>
<headline>MOROCCO BUYS 90,000 TONNES SOFT WHEAT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco overnight bought 90,000 tonnes of soft wheat for September delivery, European grain traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Of that, 60,000 tonnes were bought at $154-156 per tonne with U.S. GSM or French Coface financing, traders said.</p>
<p>Another 30,000 tonnes of soft wheat of any origin were bought at $161 per tonne and paid for in cash.</p>
<p>The wheat is due to be delivered from September 7 to September 15.  </p>
<p>Traders gave the following breakdown.</p>
<p>    30,000 tonnes Casablanca (GSM)    $154/tonne</p>
<p>				  (excluding credit costs)</p>
<p>30,000 tonnes Agadir (GSM/Coface) $156/tonne</p>
<p>				  (excluding credit costs)</p>
<p>3x10,000 tonnes Tangier/Nador/Safi $161/tonne</p>
<p>				  (cash)</p>
</text>
